From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:27:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi/phy: 7nm: determine the rate the PLL gives

determine_rate() only clamped the rate, while recalc_rate() reads back
the PLL's dec/frac: 1055977148 for 1055977248Hz. Every clk_set_rate()
of the link clocks, as msm_dsi_host_xfer_prepare() does for every
command, then finds them changed and reprograms the PLL at the rate it
runs at, relocking it mid-frame: every lane's HS FIFO underflows. The
divider searches through it also pick different out_div/bit clock
splits from one setting to the next.

Determine the rate recalc_rate() gives for the highest dec/frac not
above the rate, so a rate the PLL gives comes back as is, and compute
dec/frac rounding up, so that rate comes back to the same dec/frac.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
index 01182442dfd6..20227ed79ca7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -138,7 +138,11 @@ static void dsi_pll_calc_dec_frac(struct dsi_pll_7nm *pll, struct dsi_pll_config
 	divider = fref * 2;
 
 	multiplier = 1 << FRAC_BITS;
-	dec_multiple = div_u64(pll_freq * multiplier, divider);
+	/*
+	 * Up: a rate as determine_rate() and recalc_rate() give it, rounded
+	 * down from the PLL's dec/frac, comes back to that dec/frac
+	 */
+	dec_multiple = DIV_ROUND_UP_ULL(pll_freq * multiplier, divider);
 	dec = div_u64_rem(dec_multiple, multiplier, &frac);
 
 	if (pll->phy->cfg->quirks & DSI_PHY_7NM_QUIRK_PRE_V4_1) {
@@ -609,9 +613,21 @@ static int dsi_pll_7nm_clk_determine_rate(struct clk_hw *hw,
 					  struct clk_rate_request *req)
 {
 	struct dsi_pll_7nm *pll_7nm = to_pll_7nm(hw);
+	u64 divider = VCO_REF_CLK_RATE * 2;
+	u64 multiplier = 1 << FRAC_BITS;
+	u64 rate, dec_multiple;
+
+	rate = clamp_t(unsigned long, req->rate,
+		       pll_7nm->phy->cfg->min_pll_rate, pll_7nm->phy->cfg->max_pll_rate);
 
-	req->rate = clamp_t(unsigned long, req->rate,
-			    pll_7nm->phy->cfg->min_pll_rate, pll_7nm->phy->cfg->max_pll_rate);
+	/*
+	 * The rate the PLL gives, as recalc_rate() reads it back, for the
+	 * highest dec/frac not above the rate: a rate it gives comes back as
+	 * is, and the clock core finds a rate it already runs at unchanged,
+	 * instead of relocking it
+	 */
+	dec_multiple = DIV_ROUND_UP_ULL((rate + 1) * multiplier, divider) - 1;
+	req->rate = div_u64(dec_multiple * divider, multiplier);
 
 	return 0;
 }
